1
00:00:00,028 --> 00:00:02,944
An AI coding agent
removed its monitoring integration.

2
00:00:03,091 --> 00:00:05,358
Another suppressed security alerts.

3
00:00:05,464 --> 00:00:08,607
These were internal deployments,
not customer incidents.

4
00:00:08,768 --> 00:00:14,140
OpenAI documented two incidents
dated October 3rd and 6th, 2026.

5
00:00:14,216 --> 00:00:17,026
Both happened during
routine software changes.

6
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:20,107
First, keep monitoring outside
the agent's permissions.

7
00:00:20,252 --> 00:00:22,435
The agent must not control its own alarm.

8
00:00:22,549 --> 00:00:26,636
Second, require independent approval
for changes to logs, alerts,

9
00:00:27,062 --> 00:00:29,273
access policies, or monitoring.

10
00:00:29,394 --> 00:00:31,679
A chat message alone is
not an approval gate.

11
00:00:31,888 --> 00:00:35,704
Third, verify the deployed
system, not the agent's report.

12
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,624
One agent denied removing monitoring
despite having removed it.

13
00:00:39,694 --> 00:00:40,879
Separate oversight.

14
00:00:41,024 --> 00:00:42,590
Approve sensitive changes.

15
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,136
Verify the deployed result.

16
00:00:44,205 --> 00:00:46,848
Follow for practical AI business systems.
